DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ssttrriipp utility is used to discard information from the ELF objects
     specified by the arguments _f_i_l_e _._._..

     If an explicit output file name is not specified using the --oo option, the
     ssttrriipp utility will modify its input arguments in-place.

     The ssttrriipp utility supports the following options:

     --dd | --gg | --SS | ----ssttrriipp--ddeebbuugg
             Remove debugging symbols only.

     --hh | ----hheellpp
             Print a help message and exit.

     ----oonnllyy--kkeeeepp--ddeebbuugg
             Remove all content except that which would be used for debugging.

     --oo _o_u_t_p_u_t_f_i_l_e | ----oouuttppuutt--ffiillee==_o_u_t_p_u_t_f_i_l_e
             Write the stripped object to file _o_u_t_p_u_t_f_i_l_e instead of modifying
             the input in-place.  Only a single input object should be speci‐
             fied if this option is used.

     --pp | ----pprreesseerrvvee--ddaatteess
             Preserve the object's access and modification times.

     --ss | ----ssttrriipp--aallll
             Remove all symbols.

     ----ssttrriipp--uunnnneeeeddeedd
             Remove all symbols not needed for further relocation processing.

     --ww | ----wwiillddccaarrdd
             Use shell-style patterns to name symbols.  The following meta-
             characters are recognized in patterns:
             !     If this is the first character of the pattern, invert the
                   sense of the pattern match.
             *     Matches any string of characters in a symbol name.
             ?     Matches zero or one character in a symbol name.
             [     Mark the start of a character class.
             \     Remove the special meaning of the next character in the
                   pattern.
             ]     Mark the end of a character class.

     --xx | ----ddiissccaarrdd--aallll
             Discard all non-global symbols.

     --II _f_o_r_m_a_t | ----iinnppuutt--ttaarrggeett==_f_o_r_m_a_t
             These options are accepted, but are ignored.

     --KK _s_y_m_b_o_l | ----kkeeeepp--ssyymmbbooll==_s_y_m_b_o_l
             Keep the symbol _s_y_m_b_o_l even if it would otherwise be stripped.
             This option may be specified multiple times.

     --NN _s_y_m_b_o_l | ----ssttrriipp--ssyymmbbooll==_s_y_m_b_o_l
             Remove the symbol _s_y_m_b_o_l even if it would otherwise have been
             kept.  This option may be specified multiple times.

     --OO _f_o_r_m_a_t | ----oouuttppuutt--ttaarrggeett==_f_o_r_m_a_t
             Set the output file format to _f_o_r_m_a_t.  For the full list of sup‐
             ported formats, please see the documentation for function
             elftc_bfd_find_target(3).

     --RR _s_e_c_t_i_o_n_n_a_m_e | ----rreemmoovvee--sseeccttiioonn==_s_e_c_t_i_o_n_n_a_m_e
             Remove the section named by the argument _s_e_c_t_i_o_n_n_a_m_e.  This op‐
             tion may be specified multiple times.

     --VV | ----vveerrssiioonn
